					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "PHI\nThe Phi node gives you the Phi constant as float.\n\nExample: In this example we use Phi as part of a patch to create the golden spiral.\nThe golden spiral is a special case of the logarithmic spiral.  The formula to compute it in polar coordinates is:\nr(t) = ae^tb\n\nwhere:\ne = euler number\nt = a point in time\na = constant (scale)\nb = ln(phi) \/ (pi \/ 2)"
					}
				},
